{
  "id": "COMPOUND:25376 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "Licochalcone D is implicated in targeting SNU-387, a cell line that is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, Gypenoside Xlvi, and 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one. All these compounds are linked to the M-phase phosphoprotein 8, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the regulation of the cell cycle. The evidence indicates that Licochalcone D may act through a shared pathway that targets SNU-387, which in turn influences M-phase phosphoprotein 8. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Licochalcone D in modulating the cell cycle by targeting a common downstream effector, M-phase phosphoprotein 8. The relationship is supported by the presence of multiple compounds with overlapping targets, reinforcing the likelihood of a shared mechanism of action.",
